# Operator console

Internal HRMS data/access operator console — mounted in Backstage at `/employers` and `/dbs` (port **5001**). Next.js 16 App Router + React 19 + Ant Design 6 + Tailwind 4. Full layout is in `apps/backstage/AGENTS.md`.

```bash
npm run backstage                          # from repo root
npm run dev --workspace=apps/backstage
```

Components are `antd` only. Icons are `@ant-design/icons` only.

## Feature folders

`app/(ops)/` is a thin route map (antd providers + `/employers` / `/login` pages). Data Builder Studio is **`app/dbs/`** with its own layout — not under `(ops)`. Feature code is `features/<domain>/<capability>/` with a leaf `index.ts`. Domain folders are singular. Do not prefix the capability with the domain.

```text
# ❌ BAD
features/employee-access/employee-access-screen.tsx
features/employer-settings/
features/roles/

# ✅ GOOD
features/employee/access/access-screen.tsx
features/employer/settings/settings-screen.tsx
features/employer/roles/roles-screen.tsx
features/dbs/                    # Data Builder Studio (app-wide, not under employer)
```

- No domain-level barrel. Import `@/features/employee/access`, not `@/features/employee`.
- Same capability on two domains = two folders (`employer/roles` vs future `employee/roles`).
- App-wide login stays `features/auth/`. Data Builder Studio stays `features/dbs/`. Cross-cutting resolve stays `shared/employee/`.
- Employer URL routes stay nested under `/employers/[id]/...`. Standalone tools (dbs) use top-level ops routes.

Import with `@/`. No parent-relative `../`. Same-directory `./` is allowed.

Display dates through `@/shared/format-date`. Date-only values are `DD-MMM-YYYY`. Values with a clock time use `DD-MMM-YYYY HH:mm:ss`. Do not render raw ISO strings.

## Server Components

- Do not use dotted Ant Design subcomponents (`Typography.Title`). Import `Title` / `Text` / `Paragraph` from `@/shared/ui` or `antd/es/...`.
- Pass a serializable `items` array to `Descriptions`. Do not use `Descriptions.Item` children.
- Do not pass `render` (or other functions) in Table `columns` from a Server Component. Put the table in a `"use client"` file.
- Use Alert `title`, not deprecated `message`.
- Helper / explainer copy belongs in `PageHelp` (header info icon → modal), never a full-width banner. `AppShell` already adds the write-mode note. Feature notes: `<PageHelp source="feature-name" notes={[...]} />`. Errors and in-flow status stay as `Alert`s. Pages outside `AppShell` pass `notes` to `PageHeader`. Do not export server-only modules from the `@/shared/ui` barrel.

## Data and writes

Queries go through `@hrms/db`. Do not use `mssql` or raw SQL strings. Do not call HRMS stored procedures (`SP_AdminRoleM_*`, `SP_InsertRolePageMapping`, `sp_InsertDynamicMenuHierarchy`) from employer/employee features.

**Exception — `features/dbs` (Data Builder Studio):** may use `@hrms/database-inspector` for catalog/details and gated SP execute, and `@hrms/db` dbs helpers for SELECT-only SQL / row preview. SELECT runner is root-admin only; SP execute uses the writes gate (preview → HMAC confirm).

Employer-scoped queries include `Employerid`. Writes require `TROUBLESHOOTER_WRITES_ENABLED=1`, non-production `NODE_ENV`, and the selected env in `TROUBLESHOOTER_WRITES_ENVS`. Preview → HMAC confirm → `BEGIN TRAN` / `COMMIT`.

## Entity links

A named entity on an operator screen is an `EntityLink` from `@/shared/entity-link`. The click opens the page that already owns that entity, focused so its related rows are on screen. Status, kind, and yes/no chips stay `Tag`.

Link only when the id or name is already on the row. A label with no ref stays plain text. The same display name can be two kinds: **Bank Details** on a change request is `fieldSection` (the field catalog); **Bank Details** on an employee’s Sections list is `employeeSection` (that person’s records). Say which kind the screen means.

A new kind is one new member of `EntityRef`, one branch in `entityHref`, and one row in the table below. The destination is the existing page for that entity, focused by a route segment or query param.

A change-request id in a table opens `ChangeRequestDetailModal` on the current page (`ChangeRequestIdButton` and `useChangeRequestView`). The workflows URL stays the deep link. The id inside that open modal is plain text.

| Kind | URL | What the page shows |
|---|---|---|
| `employee` | `/employers/{id}/employees/{employmentNumber}` | Profile, plus the nav to history, sections, access, leave, and approvers |
| `employeeSection` | `/employers/{id}/employees/{employmentNumber}/sections/{sectionId}` | That person’s records for the section |
| `fieldSection` | `/employers/{id}/fields?section={name}` | Employer, Template, and Compare rows for that section |
| `field` | `/employers/{id}/fields?section={name}&field={name}` | That section, with the matching field row in view |
| `workflow` | `/employers/{id}/workflows/{workflowId}` | Header, routing tree, and scope |
| `workflowPage` | `/employers/{id}/workflows?tab=pages&page={name}` | That module page and its mapped workflows |
| `workflowGroup` | `/employers/{id}/workflows?tab=groups&group={roleId}` | Members, locations, and workflows using the group |
| `role` | `/employers/{id}/roles?roleId={roleId}` | Page grants |
| `upload` | `/employers/{id}/uploads/{uploadId}` | Sections, rows, and errors |
| `changeRequest` | `/employers/{id}/workflows?tab=requests&request={id}` | Requests tab with the detail modal open |

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — a hand-built employer path, or a plain tag for an entity
<Link href={`/employers/${employerId}/workflows/${workflowId}`}>{name}</Link>
<Tag>{sectionName}</Tag>

// ✅ GOOD
<EntityLink employerId={employerId} entity={{ kind: "workflow", workflowId }}>
  {name}
</EntityLink>
<EntityLink
  appearance="tag"
  color="blue"
  employerId={employerId}
  entity={{ kind: "fieldSection", section: sectionName }}
>
  {sectionName}
</EntityLink>

// ✅ GOOD — Pending, Added, and Yes stay tags
<Tag color="green">Added</Tag>
```
